WEBVTT

00:01.954 --> 00:02.414
Hey there.

00:03.086 --> 00:08.897
so I'm gonna show you a little bit of, one
of the things I was doing for Intercept,

00:08.932 --> 00:10.808
the, B2B agency that I was working at.

00:11.394 --> 00:15.082
So this was kind of a work in progress
over a period of time, but, what you're

00:15.083 --> 00:18.626
seeing here is the brand repo, is what
we called it, which is basically a

00:18.627 --> 00:22.298
repository with everything that you
need to get started with the new brand.

00:22.671 --> 00:27.028
we launched this new brand and reimagined
a whole bunch of things, and I came

00:27.030 --> 00:28.455
up with a bunch of concepts for that.

00:28.477 --> 00:30.403
One of them was, dynamic branding.

00:30.404 --> 00:34.252
So the logo isn't just one thing and
stays the same, it actually does a

00:34.254 --> 00:38.190
whole bunch of things and can be in
different colors and different formats,

00:38.190 --> 00:39.556
and you'll see some of that here.

00:39.556 --> 00:43.711
So this is just kind of a starting
place, downloads and guidelines and

00:43.711 --> 00:48.624
component libraries for Figma, and some
generators to generate content as well.

00:49.364 --> 00:50.507
there are some templates here.

00:50.524 --> 00:53.199
We talked about this a little
bit, the PowerPoint templates.

00:53.605 --> 00:56.470
basically, these were all generated.

00:56.529 --> 00:59.979
You know, we went in and tweaked things,
but it got better and better at doing it,

00:59.981 --> 01:04.758
so, we were able to create some basic,
template structures for, for the brand.

01:05.271 --> 01:06.414
then some fun stuff.

01:06.438 --> 01:11.109
This is kind of like a, a, a generator
for generating Teams backgrounds.

01:11.546 --> 01:15.195
you can see here, you
can randomize this thing.

01:15.205 --> 01:20.812
You can actually pull these around,
to, get a composition that you like.

01:21.208 --> 01:26.076
it also will, do video as well, so you
can have this kind of slowly morphing,

01:26.489 --> 01:27.816
background, which is kinda neat.

01:28.418 --> 01:31.220
I'm sorry if you can't see
all of it here in the screen.

01:31.222 --> 01:36.037
I'm using Loom, so I'm trying to show
you everything, in, in this window.

01:36.141 --> 01:38.548
we also did something for generating
your own LinkedIn banner so

01:38.548 --> 01:42.520
everybody can customize, their own
desktop patterns, or wallpapers.

01:42.617 --> 01:45.634
they can customize their own,
LinkedIn banners as well.

01:46.066 --> 01:49.039
we even did a thing with doing
your own email signature.

01:49.039 --> 01:51.027
so I created an application that did that.

01:51.393 --> 01:57.002
You can see here, if you hit Generate, it
generates your own unique, Intercept, logo

01:57.005 --> 01:59.053
for your… You can change colors as well.

01:59.982 --> 02:02.560
you can see the little chips and
slices kinda move around, and

02:02.560 --> 02:03.949
these are all Intercept logos.

02:03.950 --> 02:05.737
They all are the same brand.

02:06.373 --> 02:07.719
so that's kind of a neat thing.

02:07.766 --> 02:10.762
And then you're, you're able to preview
it here, what it might look like.

02:11.847 --> 02:13.176
you can see it changing here.

02:14.025 --> 02:18.317
this is a pattern generator, so just a
way to present, we call it Fritz patterns.

02:18.341 --> 02:22.233
These, this triangle motif is called
Fritz, and it's what the skill

02:22.233 --> 02:25.271
was called as well, and the brand
package, was all called Fritz.

02:25.858 --> 02:28.838
you can change patterns here.

02:28.879 --> 02:33.356
You can do a whole bunch of
interesting things, with this, just

02:33.850 --> 02:35.264
doing, patterns and backgrounds.

02:35.905 --> 02:37.312
let's see, what else do we have here?

02:37.719 --> 02:40.216
this Fritzoid animator is kinda neat.

02:40.512 --> 02:45.128
if you want an animation, you
can see how this changes, and it

02:45.128 --> 02:48.956
animates, and there's different
ways of having it cut maybe instead.

02:49.489 --> 02:53.052
You can adjust the speed, all this
kind of stuff, fun things like that.

02:53.819 --> 02:55.660
and then, assets and downloads.

02:55.663 --> 02:57.945
So this is all of the, brand guidelines.

02:57.946 --> 03:01.848
So a font package, there's
the full f- logo package.

03:02.390 --> 03:05.056
and there's some brand rules here.

03:05.348 --> 03:08.610
More of that is in the Figma kit as
well, but you can see some of it here.

03:09.217 --> 03:13.885
some photography rules, typography
rules, and then down below is,

03:13.887 --> 03:15.955
like, a full component library.

03:16.337 --> 03:22.354
So everything you could possibly want
from a UI/UX point of view is all in here.

03:23.006 --> 03:28.335
and this was all done with combination of
teaching it what the brand was, but also,

03:28.436 --> 03:30.361
going in and, and tweaking things, right?

03:30.439 --> 03:33.048
And then going back and saying, "This
is the way I actually want it done."

03:33.048 --> 03:38.873
So again, you know, we can get a lot of
the way there with AI, but, you know, it

03:38.873 --> 03:42.100
always has to have somebody at the other
end saying, "Hey, that's what's good,

03:42.100 --> 03:46.040
and that's what's not good." So it's
an, you know, an important consideration

03:46.041 --> 03:47.635
when we're doing all of this stuff.

03:48.264 --> 03:48.777
but yeah.

03:48.777 --> 03:50.654
It's a full, full, full package.

03:50.700 --> 03:52.103
a lot of work went into it.

03:52.454 --> 03:57.970
A lot of, a lot of sort of integrations
into, the workflow for the team as well.

03:58.206 --> 04:00.835
So that's what I was kind of
in progress doing, and then I

04:00.836 --> 04:02.285
handed a lot of that work over.

04:02.807 --> 04:04.279
let's see, what else can I tell you?

04:04.326 --> 04:05.265
Just some details.

04:05.266 --> 04:08.949
You know, you can go to dark mode
or light mode, things like that.

04:09.579 --> 04:10.146
but yeah.

04:10.348 --> 04:17.281
So that's kind of, the Intercept, Fritz
rebrand, and a lot of the tools and

04:17.290 --> 04:20.724
some of the fun stuff that, that I used
to, launch the brand with the team.

04:20.726 --> 04:24.549
And, and then part of this was also,
you know, of course, training people

04:24.551 --> 04:29.733
how to use the brand skill, how
to use, the Figma kit, and, yeah.

04:29.960 --> 04:34.198
And then that was all getting rolled
into a brand OS, which is another

04:34.199 --> 04:38.842
idea I had for the company, which was
basically, having a lot of these tools

04:38.842 --> 04:40.617
live in a centralized kind of place.

04:40.925 --> 04:43.858
So it's not just a brand repo where
they go and pull stuff down, but

04:43.862 --> 04:47.331
a, an actually integrated piece of
software with the, with the company.

04:47.509 --> 04:49.923
So I hope that kind of
gives you a good overview.

04:49.923 --> 04:54.802
I'm happy to like, you know, walk through
this more in person or, or on screen.

04:54.965 --> 04:59.731
but, hopefully that, that helps you, get a
sense of, some of the things I was up to.

04:59.899 --> 05:01.464
anyways, it was great
talking with you today.

05:01.512 --> 05:02.652
hope to talk to you soon.

05:03.395 --> 05:03.642
Bye.
